      generic: "trospium",
      aliases: ["Sanctura", "trospium chloride", "quaternary bladder antimuscarinic", "trospum", "tropium bladder"],
      brandExamples: ["Sanctura"],
      class: "Quaternary-ammonium peripheral antimuscarinic; predominantly renal elimination",
      usedToTreat: "Adult overactive bladder with urgency, frequency and urge urinary incontinence.",
      description: "Trospium is a positively charged quaternary antimuscarinic that reduces detrusor contraction but crosses lipid membranes and the blood-brain barrier less readily than tertiary agents. That can reduce, not abolish, CNS exposure. It undergoes little CYP metabolism and is substantially excreted by the kidney, making renal function and empty-stomach administration more important than CYP interaction management.",
